---
import Gallery from '../../layouts/Gallery.astro';
import Related from '../../components/Related.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const tiers = `/* Tier 1 — raw palette: never consumed by components */
--bo-palette-blue-600: #2563eb;

/* Tier 2 — semantic roles: what components reference; dark theme
   redefines THIS tier under [data-theme="dark"] */
--bo-color-accent: var(--bo-palette-blue-600);
--bo-color-accent-solid: var(--bo-palette-blue-600); /* carries white text, both themes */
--bo-color-accent-text: var(--bo-palette-blue-700);  /* sits on accent-subtle, >= 4.5:1 */

/* Tier 3 — density aliases: remapped by [data-density], the ONLY sizing
   source components use internally */
--bo-density-row-height: 2.5rem;

/* Tier 4 — component-local: defaults to globals, variants override locally */
.bo-btn { --bo-btn-bg: var(--bo-color-accent-solid); }`;
---
<Gallery title="Design tokens">
  <p class="demo-note">
    Four tiers, each with one job. Components never touch the raw palette; brands
    never touch component files. The tier boundaries are what make dark mode,
    density, and re-branding one-attribute or one-file operations.
  </p>
  <section class="demo">
    <h2>The four tiers</h2>
    <pre><code>{tiers}</code></pre>
    <p>Token <strong>roles encode contrast guarantees</strong>: <code>*-solid</code>
    backgrounds carry white text in both themes (≥ 4.5:1, never dark-remapped);
    <code>*-text</code> foregrounds sit on <code>*-subtle</code> backgrounds
    (≥ 4.5:1, remapped to light steps in dark mode). Every pair is
    <a href={base + '/reference/tokens'}>computed and CI-gated on every build</a>
    — every resolved value, both themes, in the
    <a href={base + '/reference/tokens'}>token reference</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Unit doctrine</h2>
    <ul class="bo-stack bo-stack--tight docs-list">
      <li><strong>rem</strong> for space and size — tracks the user's font preference. Density is rem-only; px overrides of density tokens are unsupported (they clip text when users raise the root font).</li>
      <li><strong>px</strong> only for hairlines (borders, focus rings, connectors) — visual weight must not scale; integer px + single-edge borders is also the 125% display-scaling mitigation.</li>
      <li><strong>ch</strong> for mono-measured content and docs prose only — always a minimum width, never in a token consumed across font contexts, never in print.</li>
      <li>Container-query thresholds in <strong>rem</strong>; <code>pt</code> only inside <code>@media print</code>; line-height unitless.</li>
      <li>Heights are <strong>minimums</strong> (<code>min-height</code>) — fixed heights clip under WCAG text-spacing overrides.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Constraint: the framework assumes an unmodified root
    font-size. Hosts that rescale <code>html</code> (legacy 62.5% hacks) rescale
    everything — embed via iframe instead.</p>
  </section>
  <Related links={[["/reference/tokens", "Token reference (all values)"], ["/concepts/density", "Density"], ["/concepts/cascade", "Cascade contract"], ["/base/colors", "Color scales"]]} />
</Gallery>
